      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To evaluate two-year results of using a metallic stent EPHESOS in patients with native atherosclerotic lesion of coronary arteries (without prior interventions)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "The stent was implanted to 731 patients. 53% had manifestations of unstable angina. 42% of the lesions were complicated. The length of the stenosis was 15.5 +/- 6.8 mm, 44% stenoses were long."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The success of stenting was 99.6%. Cases of acute and subacute thrombosis were absent. Non-Q wave myocardial infarction in primary hospitalization developed in 4 patients. For 6 months, cardiovascular complications (death, angina, restenosis, repeated revascularization) occurred in 21%. Angiographic control follow-up of 6 months maximum covered 329 (45%) patients. Hemodynamically significant restenosis was detected in 18% patients. Cardiovascular complications for 24 months occurred in 39%."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The EPHESOS stent has demonstrated a stable long-term effect on prevention of thrombosis and restenosis in the majority of patients with a relatively high risk of intervention."
        }
      ]},
